---
import Base from "../layouts/Base.astro";

// Describes what this SITE actually does today, which is very little. When the
// product launches and there are accounts, this page needs rewriting rather
// than amending — an inaccurate privacy policy is worse than none.
const updated = "30 August 2026";
---

<Base
  title="Privacy — PaceStreak"
  description="What PaceStreak collects on this website: no analytics, no tracking, no third-party scripts. What happens when you email us."
  path="/privacy"
>
  <section class="py-16 sm:py-20">
    <div class="wrap max-w-2xl">
      <p class="eyebrow">Privacy</p>
      <h1 class="mt-3 text-4xl font-semibold tracking-tight">Privacy</h1>
      <p class="mt-4 text-[0.92rem] text-dim">Last updated {updated}</p>

      <div class="prose-page mt-10">
        <p>
          This page describes <strong>this website</strong>. PaceStreak the
          product is not released yet; when it is, and there are accounts and
          training data, this page will be rewritten rather than quietly
          extended.
        </p>

        <h2>What this site collects</h2>
        <p>
          Nothing. There is no analytics, no tracking pixel, no advertising
          network, no session cookie and no third-party script of any kind.
        </p>
        <p>
          That is not only a policy. The site ships a{" "}
          <strong>Content Security Policy</strong> of{" "}
          <code>default-src 'self'</code>, which means the browser blocks any
          request to another origin outright. If someone added a tracker, it
          would not work.
        </p>

        <h2>What happens automatically</h2>
        <p>
          The site is served by Cloudflare Pages. Like every web server,
          Cloudflare's infrastructure processes the information needed to
          deliver a page — your IP address, the page requested, your browser's
          user agent — and keeps operational logs. We do not receive analytics,
          per-visitor reports, or any profile built from that traffic.
        </p>
        <p>
          Uptime monitoring at{" "}
          <a href="https://status.pacestreak.com">status.pacestreak.com</a>{" "}
          checks whether the site responds. It records the site's own
          availability, not visitors.
        </p>

        <h2>If you email us</h2>
        <p>
          Mail sent to <a href="mailto:hello@pacestreak.com"
            >hello@pacestreak.com</a
          > is received through Zoho Mail and read by a person. If you ask to be
          on the early access list, we keep your address for that one purpose:
          to email you once, when it opens.
        </p>
        <p>
          We do not sell it, share it, or add it to a newsletter. Ask us to
          delete it and we will, in full.
        </p>

        <h2>What is stored in your browser</h2>
        <p>
          Nothing. No cookies are set by this site, and nothing is written to
          local storage.
        </p>

        <h2>Your rights</h2>
        <p>
          Because the only personal data held is an email address you sent us
          voluntarily, exercising your rights is straightforward: write to{" "}
          <a href="mailto:hello@pacestreak.com">hello@pacestreak.com</a> and ask
          what we hold, ask for a copy, or ask us to erase it.
        </p>

        <h2>Changes</h2>
        <p>
          This page is versioned publicly in{" "}
          <a href="https://github.com/PaceStreak">the repository</a>, so any
          change to it has a commit and a date attached.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
</Base>
